  "body": "### What is the issue with the Streams Standard?\n\nThey are usually created by getReader and getWriter, but they also have public constructors that receives streams.\n\nThe spec says it's just equivalent to getReader/Writer but it can lead to weird lifecycle situation where the reader is from a different realm than the stream's:\n\n```js\nnew ReadableStreamDefaultReader(new (window.open().ReadableStream)());\n```\n\nThis makes Gecko do extra works here and there (because whatever the stream produces can be in a different realm too), but I wonder it's worth at all?",
